course: dictionary
lesson: 904
title: Bitumen: the sticky black road material
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Bitumen is a black, sticky substance made from oil, a bit like tar. You may not know the word, but the sentences around it give clues. «At the bottom is hard-rolled crushed stone that spreads the weight of lorries, and on top is asphalt, a hot mix of small stones and sticky black bitumen.» The words sticky and black tell you what bitumen looks and feels like.
explain: The second sentence helps even more. «A road is built in layers: crushed stone rolled hard at the bottom, then hot asphalt, a mix of stones and sticky black bitumen, spread and rolled flat on top.» Bitumen is one part of the mix, and it is spread while the mix is hot. So bitumen must be a material that is sticky when hot and used to make a surface.
explain: Words can mean different things in different places. In Australia and New Zealand, people say «the bitumen» to mean a sealed road, the kind with a smooth black surface, compared with a dirt road. Context is the best clue: if the sentence is about roads, the bitumen is the road surface, not a part of the body or a bird.
fact: Bitumen is a black, sticky, tar-like substance made from oil.
fact: Bitumen is used to make road surfaces and waterproof roofs.
fact: Bitumen is sticky and soft when hot, and hard when it cools.
fact: In Australia and New Zealand, «the bitumen» means a sealed road.
fact: Bitumen is an uncountable noun, so we say «some bitumen», not «a bitumen» or «three bitumens».
exercise: What is bitumen? | A hot drink made from beans | A metal used for building bridges | *A black, sticky, tar-like substance made from oil | A hard grey stone used at the bottom of a road
exercise: In «asphalt, a hot mix of small stones and sticky black bitumen», what is mixed with the small stones? | Sand | Water | *Bitumen | Crushed stone
exercise: In Australia, what does «the bitumen» mean? | A kind of bird | *The tarred surface of a road | A sandy beach | A roof that leaks
test: Why is bitumen used on roofs? | *It is waterproof | It makes roofs warm to touch | It makes roofs see-through | It makes roofs float on water
test: Which layer goes at the bottom of a road? | Hot asphalt | Bitumen poured on its own | Sand spread flat | *Crushed stone rolled hard
exam: Ella says bitumen is a kind of stone. Is she right? | Yes, it is a metal used for bridges | Yes, it is a hard grey stone | No, it is a plant that grows on roads | *No, it is a sticky black substance made from oil
